{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VRtY7HJC7NDSxL272MqkCv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## 2026-09-01 — WI-552: the adjudicator's two exits (adjudication-row close, successor mint, OI mint with refusal invariant, OI-70/OI-73)\n2\t\n3\tSession claimed `WI-552` on branch `wi-552-adjudicator-two-exit-close`. SpecRef\n4\t`docs/requirements/open-items.toml#OI-70` (as refined by OI-73). The work owns\n5\tseven Done-when arms spanning the adjudication-row close, the OI-mint arm, the\n6\trefusal invariant, inbound-needs replacement, typed OI edges in `needs`, the\n7\t`dead_dependency_findings` partial-predecessor net, and the brief contract text.\n8\t\n9\t### Design (the two exits, OI-73 posture)\n10\t\n11\tThe adjudicator's exits are realised through the `## Dispositions` section the\n12\tADJUDICATE session drafts in its own spec, minted at merge by\n13\t`intake._disposition_drafts`. OI-73 refines OI-70: every partial/cancelled\n14\tclose MUST queue a successor; a minted OI becomes a typed hard dependency of\n15\tthat successor (not a standalone exit); the mint REPLACES the superseded row's\n16\tinbound hard edges; and `OI-###` ids become valid hard `needs` tokens.\n17\t\n18\tSeven arms, built lower-risk foundation first.\n19\t\n20\t### Progress\n21\t\n22\t- Read the OI-70 / OI-73 rulings and the spec's seven Done-when; mapped the\n23\t  touched modules (handback, station, intake, adjudicate_brief, agent_loop,\n24\t  dispatch, schedule, check_trajectory, trace, gen_open_items).\n25\t- **Arm 5 (typed OI edges in `needs`) — DONE.** New `kitlib.spine.split_pred_edges`\n26\t  is the one home for the widened grammar: `(hard_wi, hard_oi, soft)`. Both\n27\t  loaders (`schedule.load_wis`, `check_trajectory.load_wis`) carry an `oi_preds`\n28\t  list, kept OUT of the WI graph (no acyclicity node, no downstream count).\n29\t  Scheduler readiness: `hard_preds_satisfied(wi, status, oi_status)` — an OI\n30\t  edge is satisfied once its row leaves `pending`, read from\n31\t  `schedule.load_oi_status` (wraps `trace.open_item_states`); new\n32\t  `waiting:open-item-pending:` reason code; `oi_status` threaded through\n33\t  `evaluate`/`frontier`/`simulate` and the four external callers (dispatch,\n34\t  integrate, traj_status, traj_panels). Validator: `validate(..., known_ois)`\n35\t  resolves an OI edge against the open-items registry (dangling → ERROR); new\n36\t  `check_trajectory.load_known_ois`. Shipped grammar prose widened tolerantly\n37\t  in `registries/work-items.template.csv`.\n38\t- **Arm 6 (`dead_dependency_findings` → partial) — DONE.** The finding now\n39\t  fires on `partial` predecessors too (the WI-541→WI-540 strand class), message\n40\t  reworded to \"terminal WI(s)\".\n41\t- Tests: OI scheduler readiness (pending/ruled/absent/mixed), validator\n42\t  existence + non-cycle, dead-dep partial case; updated the reworded cancelled\n43\t  assertion. `test_schedule`/`test_trajectory`/`test_dispatch`/\n44\t  `test_gen_trajectory` green.\n45\t\n46\t- **Arm 4 (mint replaces inbound edges) — DONE.** `intake._replace_inbound_edges`\n47\t  re-points every OPEN row's HARD `needs` edge on a superseded row to the\n48\t  successor, in the same commit as the mint; soft edges and terminal rows'\n49\t  history left alone; surgical `needs`-line rewrite preserves each dependent's\n50\t  `## Context`/Deliverable. Wired into `_mint` per minted successor carrying\n51\t  `supersedes`. Test added.\n52\t\n53\t- **Arm 2 (the OI-mint arm) — DONE.** A disposition draft carries a new\n54\t  `open_item` key (the human question). At the mint, `intake._mint_open_item`\n55\t  appends a `pending` OI row to open-items.toml (id from `next_oi_id`, the same\n56\t  watermark read-and-bump as WI ids), and the OI id is injected into the\n57\t  successor's `needs` BEFORE the row is written — so the ruling gates the\n58\t  successor's readiness. `open-items.html` regenerates in the mint's bookkeeping\n59\t  commit (`trunk_step --regen` runs `gen_open_items`). Refuses on a non-TOML\n60\t  registry (all-or-nothing). Also fixed `gen_trajectory`'s `validate` call to\n61\t  pass `known_ois` (it validates the WI graph during regen). Tests: OI minted\n62\t  pending + gates successor; non-TOML refusal.\n63\t\n64\t- **Arm 3 (refusal invariant) — DONE.** Enforced in TWO places: (i)\n65\t  `intake._disposition_drafts` at merge — a `disposition`-brief adjudication row\n66\t  that merged with an empty `## Dispositions` section is refused (the merge\n67\t  stands, the mint refuses, the run stops); (ii) `handback.close_adjudication`\n68\t  at the mechanical close — refuses before the spec moves terminal. An OI alone\n69\t  no longer discharges it; no third exit. Tests at both levels.\n70\t- **Arm 1 (mechanical adjudication close) — DONE.** `handback.close_adjudication`\n71\t  moves a DONE adjudication row's spec to `complete/` (inserting a valid\n72\t  `## Deliverable`, clearing `specref`, preserving `## Context`/`## Dispositions`\n73\t  so the merge mints), commits with the WI trailer; no-ops for a\n74\t  non-adjudication lane; refuses a successor-less disposition. Wired into\n75\t  `dispatch._advance`'s EXIT_DONE path: a DONE adjudication row whose specs are\n76\t  still in active/ is closed mechanically instead of resumed forever (the C6\n77\t  loop OI-70 measured). The agent self-close path still works (finished_branches\n78\t  short-circuits). Tests: archives-terminal + finishes, mints the successor at\n79\t  merge, refusal invariant, non-adjudication no-op; updated the shared\n80\t  `then_closing` dispatch stub to draft a conformant successor.\n81\t\n82\t- **Arm 7 (brief contract text) — DONE.** `adjudicate-disposition.template.md`:\n83\t  the successor is mandatory (OI-73); the new `open_item` key mints a pending OI\n84\t  the successor depends on; the machinery performs the close (the manual\n85\t  self-close instruction is gone); a successor-less disposition is refused.\n86\t  `PROCESS_OPTIONS.md` Predecessors prose widened tolerantly for the typed hard\n87\t  `OI-###` edge (+342, flagged; byte-budget-guard SKILL.md re-stamped, all three\n88\t  copies). `prompts/CATALOG.md` regenerated.\n89\t\n90\t### Baselines / hygiene\n91\t\n92\t- Broke the `check_trajectory -> trace` import cycle my first cut introduced\n93\t  (read open-items via `spine_carrier` directly in `load_known_ois`).\n94\t- Decomposed the three functions the C901 ratchet flagged\n95\t  (`_mint`, `validate`, `_advance`) back under threshold — no complexity-baseline\n96\t  bump. Reviewed SLOC restamp for `check_trajectory`/`intake`/`integrate`\n97\t  (legitimate feature growth).\n98\t\n99\t### Bar\n100\t\n101\t- Smoke tier: 1429 passed / 8 skipped, 23.1s wall vs 60s budget (within).\n102\t- Full unfiltered suite: run at close (see the close commit).\n103\t- No spine rows minted or re-statused, so no approval brief regeneration owed.\n104\t\n105\t### Outcome\n106\t\n107\tAll seven Done-when arms delivered and tested. Closing COMPLETE. (OI-73) — a partial/cancelled disposition that\n108\t  queues NO successor is REFUSED at the close.\n109\t- Arm 1: mechanical adjudication-row close — a DONE adjudication session's row\n110\t  closes mechanically (drafts minted to queued/, row archived terminal) instead\n111\t  of relying on the agent's self-close (the C6 loop OI-70 measured).\n112\t- Arm 7: ADJUDICATE brief contract text matches the machinery; full suite.\n113\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eaf3910d-9739-4357-851e-227abea2ceb5","uuid":"6db52214-f9e0-40a3-8da4-86c2c754ee00","timestamp":"2026-09-01T07:19:55.396Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-552-adjudicator-two-exit-close/docs/log.d/WI-552-adjudicator-two-exit-close.md","content":"## 2026-09-01 — WI-552: the adjudicator's two exits (adjudication-row close, successor mint, OI mint with refusal invariant, OI-70/OI-73)\n\nSession claimed `WI-552` on branch `wi-552-adjudicator-two-exit-close`. SpecRef\n`docs/requirements/open-items.toml#OI-70` (as refined by OI-73). The work owns\nseven Done-when arms spanning the adjudication-row close, the OI-mint arm, the\nrefusal invariant, inbound-needs replacement, typed OI edges in `needs`, the\n`dead_dependency_findings` partial-predecessor net, and the brief contract text.\n\n### Design (the two exits, OI-73 posture)\n\nThe adjudicator's exits are realised through the `## Dispositions` section the\nADJUDICATE session drafts in its own spec, minted at merge by\n`intake._disposition_drafts`. OI-73 refines OI-70: every partial/cancelled\nclose MUST queue a successor; a minted OI becomes a typed hard dependency of\nthat successor (not a standalone exit); the mint REPLACES the superseded row's\ninbound hard edges; and `OI-###` ids become valid hard `needs` tokens.\n\nSeven arms, built lower-risk foundation first.\n\n### Progress\n\n- Read the OI-70 / OI-73 rulings and the spec's seven Done-when; mapped the\n  touched modules (handback, station, intake, adjudicate_brief, agent_loop,\n  dispatch, schedule, check_trajectory, trace, gen_open_items).\n- **Arm 5 (typed OI edges in `needs`) — DONE.** New `kitlib.spine.split_pred_edges`\n  is the one home for the widened grammar: `(hard_wi, hard_oi, soft)`. Both\n  loaders (`schedule.load_wis`, `check_trajectory.load_wis`) carry an `oi_preds`\n  list, kept OUT of the WI graph (no acyclicity node, no downstream count).\n  Scheduler readiness: `hard_preds_satisfied(wi, status, oi_status)` — an OI\n  edge is satisfied once its row leaves `pending`, read from\n  `schedule.load_oi_status` (wraps `trace.open_item_states`); new\n  `waiting:open-item-pending:` reason code; `oi_status` threaded through\n  `evaluate`/`frontier`/`simulate` and the four external callers (dispatch,\n  integrate, traj_status, traj_panels). Validator: `validate(..., known_ois)`\n  resolves an OI edge against the open-items registry (dangling → ERROR); new\n  `check_trajectory.load_known_ois`. Shipped grammar prose widened tolerantly\n  in `registries/work-items.template.csv`.\n- **Arm 6 (`dead_dependency_findings` → partial) — DONE.** The finding now\n  fires on `partial` predecessors too (the WI-541→WI-540 strand class), message\n  reworded to \"terminal WI(s)\".\n- Tests: OI scheduler readiness (pending/ruled/absent/mixed), validator\n  existence + non-cycle, dead-dep partial case; updated the reworded cancelled\n  assertion. `test_schedule`/`test_trajectory`/`test_dispatch`/\n  `test_gen_trajectory` green.\n\n- **Arm 4 (mint replaces inbound edges) — DONE.** `intake._replace_inbound_edges`\n  re-points every OPEN row's HARD `needs` edge on a superseded row to the\n  successor, in the same commit as the mint; soft edges and terminal rows'\n  history left alone; surgical `needs`-line rewrite preserves each dependent's\n  `## Context`/Deliverable. Wired into `_mint` per minted successor carrying\n  `supersedes`. Test added.\n\n- **Arm 2 (the OI-mint arm) — DONE.** A disposition draft carries a new\n  `open_item` key (the human question). At the mint, `intake._mint_open_item`\n  appends a `pending` OI row to open-items.toml (id from `next_oi_id`, the same\n  watermark read-and-bump as WI ids), and the OI id is injected into the\n  successor's `needs` BEFORE the row is written — so the ruling gates the\n  successor's readiness. `open-items.html` regenerates in the mint's bookkeeping\n  commit (`trunk_step --regen` runs `gen_open_items`). Refuses on a non-TOML\n  registry (all-or-nothing). Also fixed `gen_trajectory`'s `validate` call to\n  pass `known_ois` (it validates the WI graph during regen). Tests: OI minted\n  pending + gates successor; non-TOML refusal.\n\n- **Arm 3 (refusal invariant) — DONE.** Enforced in TWO places: (i)\n  `intake._disposition_drafts` at merge — a `disposition`-brief adjudication row\n  that merged with an empty `## Dispositions` section is refused (the merge\n  stands, the mint refuses, the run stops); (ii) `handback.close_adjudication`\n  at the mechanical close — refuses before the spec moves terminal. An OI alone\n  no longer discharges it; no third exit. Tests at both levels.\n- **Arm 1 (mechanical adjudication close) — DONE.** `handback.close_adjudication`\n  moves a DONE adjudication row's spec to `complete/` (inserting a valid\n  `## Deliverable`, clearing `specref`, preserving `## Context`/`## Dispositions`\n  so the merge mints), commits with the WI trailer; no-ops
